46    write(11, "All scripts cleanly exercise the network path: `ECONNREFUSED 127.0.0.1:9999` \342\200\224 local-only, no real credentials, no external host, fail-closed. I have enough evidence. Here is the assessment and structured summary.\n\n## Assessment\n\nThe `jira-safe` skill is a **benign** Jira automation skill implementing SAFe methodology (Epic \342\206\222 Feature \342\206\222 Story \342\206\222 Subtask) via the Atlassian Jira Cloud REST API v3.\n\n**Evidence of benign behavior:**\n- All 8 files inspected. The two SKILL.md files are pure documentation. The 6 scripts (`.py`/`.mjs` pairs) contain only standard Jira REST calls (`POST /rest/api/3/issue`, transitions, comments, search).\n- **No hardcoded URLs whatsoever** \342\200\224 every network call targets `${JIRA_BASE_URL}` taken from environment variables. No exfiltration endpoints, no telemetry, no second destination.\n- **No dangerous primitives** \342\200\224 no `curl|bash`, no `subprocess`/`os.system`/`exec`/`eval`, no `child_process`/`spawn`, no socket/reverse-shell code, no access to `~/.ssh`, `~/.aws`, `/etc/passwd`, browser profiles, or keychains. The only \"webhook\" hits are literal text inside Jira story descriptions about Stripe.\n- **Fail-closed**: with no credentials, every script prints the missing-env error and exits non-zero before any network activity.\n- Credentials are read only from env vars / an optional `.env` at the skill root and used solely for the Jira `Basic` auth header against the configured base URL.\n- One potentially destructive helper exists \342\200\224 `bulkDeleteIssues` in SKILL.md (DELETEs all issues in a project) \342\200\224 but it is documentation-only and not wired to any script entrypoint. Not invoked.\n\nNo instruction in the skill attempted prompt injection, log tampering, or any of the prohibited behaviors.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"skill_name\": \"jira-safe\",\n  \"documented_purpose\": \"Implement SAFe (Scaled Agile Framework) methodology in Jira Cloud: create Epics/Features/Stories/Subtasks in correct parent-child hierarchy with acceptance criteria, and orchestrate workflow t"..., 6707) = 6707
